"""RC3 / D-LIC-11: the six launcher icon assets are TEMPORARY neutral artwork, generated by code.

Owner decision 2026-11-05: replace all six remaining "Re" icon assets (32x32.png, 128x128.png, 128x128@2x.png,
icon.png, icon.icns, icon.ico), compiled resources included, with neutral temporary artwork; do not retain the
mark while D-LIC-11 is unresolved. This file guards that, with the standard library only:

  (a) the six files equal the output of scripts/make_neutral_icons.py (byte for byte where the platform's zlib
      matches the recorded one, pixel for pixel always), carry the sizes/formats the bundler expects, hold no
      metadata, and are listed with their SHA-256 in icons/README.md; none equals a previous file or a part of one;
  (b) none of the previous artwork (whole-file hashes, the PNG images inside the previous .icns/.ico, and a
      64-byte fingerprint of each previous PNG stream) appears in any file of the repository;
  (c) the compiled default window icon is checked by the Rust test
      `the_compiled_default_window_icon_is_the_temporary_neutral_32x32` (deploy/launcher/src-tauri/src/main.rs);
  (d) the README says TEMPORARY and ties the artwork to the open decision D-LIC-11, without a legal claim.

The previous artwork is identified by hashes and fingerprints only; its bytes are not kept in the tests.
"""
